# Product writing

Use em dashes sparingly in app and website copy, generated agent replies,
code comments, and new documentation. Prefer a short sentence, comma, colon,
or parentheses when it reads naturally. Use a middle dot or colon for compact
UI labels and a vertical bar for page-title separators.

Rewrite for clarity rather than replacing every dash mechanically. Preserve
user-authored content, exact quotations and third-party attribution, technical
syntax, identifiers, API values and historical evidence. Do not alter a public
contract or an idempotent request payload solely to change punctuation.

Example: “Tell us in your own words, or leave this for later.”
